📱🔭 US tech giants look to go off-grid to power AI boom

Amazon, Microsoft and Oracle are among the companies turning to their own power generation as yearslong waits for grid connections threaten to delay data center projects, Bloomberg reports.

🔴 Around a quarter of planned US data center capacity is expected to have on-site power generation;

🔴 Natural gas is emerging as the leading option for round-the-clock electricity, while some developers are exploring solar, batteries and small nuclear reactors;

🔴 Gas turbine costs have more than doubled, with delivery times stretching beyond five years;

🔴 The shift could drive up US power-sector emissions, with planned off-grid gas plants potentially adding 152 million metric tons of CO₂ annually by 2035 compared with grid-powered data centers, according to BloombergNEF estimates.

The push to generate their own electricity could help tech giants bypass grid bottlenecks — but risks creating a more expensive and polluting energy landscape.

